13","local":{}},"aliases":["Y13","Upper Sixth"],"voiceOnly":false}],"until":null,"notes":"School is compulsory from the start of the academic year a child turns 5 (Reception, the Foundation Stage, left out as for England) until late May of the year they turn 16. DESC names the years Reception and Years 1–13 in England's key stages, with Years 12–13 as an optional Key Stage 5 in school sixth forms; University College Isle of Man offers other post-16 courses. There are no key stage SATs; GCSEs and IGCSEs come in Years 10–11 and A levels in sixth form. The curriculum is partly drawn from England's. desc.gov.im refused our requests, so it is cited from the Web Archive."}]
